{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a67733726c4ae5e8","name":"Flare-S Swoop","source":{"id":"source:reference-a67733726c4ae5e8","title":"Flare-S Swoop","revision":19443,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:59:04Z","sha256":"f0d7e644ac75594e5412bb458353cb19f29687a3be5a53a230da8fb6ade48c7a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19443","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Flare-S%20Swoop&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a67733726c4ae5e8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Mobquet Flare-S is considered by many to be the perfect Swoop Bike. After the New Order outlawed Podracing, those who wanted to engage in high-speed, high-risk sports turned to swoop racing, and the Flare-S quickly became the most common Swoop Bike on the race circuit. The Flare-S is extremely powerful, has a maximum altitude of 350 meters (it can be modified with a DC 15 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check to reach an altitude of several kilometers), and is much faster than standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeder Bikes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeder_Bikes"},". It is also extremely dangerous to fly, with few safety systems. Professional swoop racers sometimes add deflectors to their bikes (granting them SR 5), but doing so is an expensive modification, running 20,000 credits, and rarely saves lives.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Flare-S is also popular with gangs, mercenaries and bounty hunters. A \"swoop culture\" of high-risk, stunt-oriented behavior exists on many worlds, and the dividing line between amateur swoop racers and criminally minded swoop gangs is often fuzzy. The Flare-S has sufficient power to mount ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"}," (though not in addition to deflectors) and is sturdy enough that many survive longer than their riders.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Flare-S Swoop Statistics (CL 3)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 15; +2 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 50; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 5; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 20\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 12 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Character Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charac